      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-root ds-side\"><button class=\"ds-nav active\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"128\" cy=\"96\" r=\"56\"/><path d=\"M32 216c16-40 56-64 96-64s80 24 96 64Z\"/></svg>Invitados</button><button class=\"ds-nav\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"128\" cy=\"128\" r=\"88\"/><path d=\"M128 40v88l76 44\"/></svg>Respuestas</button><button class=\"ds-nav\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M64 120V64a24 24 0 0 1 24-24h80a24 24 0 0 1 24 24v56M40 120h176v48H40ZM64 168v48M192 168v48\"/></svg>Mesas</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-root{--ink:#1d2436;--navy:#2b3653;--navy-hover:#222b43;--navy-soft:#eef0f5;--corinto:#6b1620;--bg:#f6f4ef;--surface:#fff;--surface-2:#faf8f4;--line:#e6e1d7;--line-strong:#d5cdbf;--text-2:#555c6e;--text-3:#868b98;--ok:#2f6b4f;--ok-soft:#e7f1eb;--wait:#93640f;--wait-soft:#f8efdc;--no:#6e6860;--no-soft:#efece7;--r-sm:8px;--r-md:12px;--r-lg:16px;--r-full:999px;--shadow-1:0 1px 2px rgba(29,36,54,.05);--ease:cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);font-family:Montserrat,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink);}.ds-side{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;width:220px;padding:.9rem;background:var(--surface-2);border-right:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.7rem;min-height:40px;padding:.5rem .75rem;border:0;border-radius:var(--r-sm);background:transparent;color:var(--text-2);font:500 .875rem Montserrat,system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;transition:background 140ms var(--ease),color 140ms var(--ease)}.ds-nav:hover{background:rgba(29,36,54,.05);color:var(--ink)}.ds-nav.active{background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;box-shadow:var(--shadow-1),inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line)}.ds-nav.active svg{color:var(--corinto)}.ds-nav:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--navy);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Response Summary",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "Signature: serif headline count plus one proportional sage/amber/stone bar.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-root\"><section class=\"ds-card\"><div class=\"ds-head\"><p class=\"ds-big\">64</p><div><p class=\"ds-big-label\">personas vienen</p><p class=\"ds-sub\">de 112 invitadas</p></div></div><div class=\"ds-bar\"><span style=\"flex-grow:64;background:var(--ok)\"></span><span style=\"flex-grow:36;background:#d9a441\"></span><span style=\"flex-grow:12;background:#b5aea4\"></span></div></section></div>",
      "css": ".ds-root{--ink:#1d2436;--navy:#2b3653;--navy-hover:#222b43;--navy-soft:#eef0f5;--corinto:#6b1620;--bg:#f6f4ef;--surface:#fff;--surface-2:#faf8f4;--line:#e6e1d7;--line-strong:#d5cdbf;--text-2:#555c6e;--text-3:#868b98;--ok:#2f6b4f;--ok-soft:#e7f1eb;--wait:#93640f;--wait-soft:#f8efdc;--no:#6e6860;--no-soft:#efece7;--r-sm:8px;--r-md:12px;--r-lg:16px;--r-full:999px;--shadow-1:0 1px 2px rgba(29,36,54,.05);--ease:cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);font-family:Montserrat,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink);}.ds-card{display:grid;gap:1.25rem;max-width:520px;padding:1.5rem;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--r-lg);box-shadow:var(--shadow-1)}.ds-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem}.ds-big{margin:0;font:600 4rem/0.9 'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-big-label{margin:0;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600}.ds-sub{margin:.15rem 0 0;font-size:.8125rem;color:var(--text-2)}.ds-bar{display:flex;gap:3px;height:14px;border-radius:var(--r-full);overflow:hidden;background:var(--no-soft)}.ds-bar span{flex-basis:0;min-width:6px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Wedding Planner's Desk",
    "overview": "The category-standard dashboard (side navigation, a summary, a table) played straight, at the finish of Linear, Stripe Dashboard, Zola and Airbnb hosting, in a friendly register for two non-technical people managing their own wedding, mostly on a phone. Nothing is ironic or novel about the structure; the character comes from the wedding's own materials: warm off-white paper, navy ink, a single corinto mark, a serif reserved for titles.\n\nDensity is moderate: a 14px Montserrat base, 38–42px controls, generous card padding. White surfaces sit on warm paper with a hairline and a whisper of ink-tinted shadow. Attendance status is the one piece of color semantics, and it never changes: sage for coming, amber for waiting, stone for not coming. The login card adds a faint corinto radial glow (6% corinto) on the paper. The rejected reference is the copied predecessor panel: a dark blue slab with emoji and loose, unrelated cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper background, white surfaces, hairline borders, soft ink-tinted shadows.",
      "Navy carries text and the primary action; corinto appears only as brand mark and selection.",
      "Three fixed attendance colors, used identically in badges, dots, bars and legends.",
      "Montserrat for all interface text with lining and tabular figures; Cormorant Garamond only for titles and the headline count.",
      "Phosphor single-stroke icons (regular, filled when active); zero emoji.",
      "Desktop sidebar, phone top bar plus thumb-reach tab bar, phone dialogs as bottom sheets."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three States Rule",
        "body": "Attendance is always and only sage (coming), amber (waiting), stone (not coming), in that order, everywhere: badge, dot, bar segment, legend, filter. No other hue may mean a status.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Corinto Is A Seal Rule",
        "body": "Corinto marks brand and current selection (monogram tile, active nav icon, active tab). It is never a button fill, a link color or a status.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink-Tinted Rule",
        "body": "Hover washes, overlays and shadows derive from ink (`rgba(29,36,54,α)`), never neutral black, so depth stays warm on paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Names, Sans Operates Rule",
        "body": "Cormorant Garamond appears only in titles, names and the headline count. Every control, number in a table, and label is Montserrat.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Count Rule",
        "body": "Any number that is compared or totaled (counts, seats, pills, legends) uses tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline First Rule",
        "body": "Every surface carries a 1px hairline; the shadow only softens it. A surface with shadow and no border is off-system.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** scope every admin style under `.adm-theme` and read values from its custom properties.",
      "**Do** express attendance only through sage, amber and stone, in that order.",
      "**Do** use Phosphor icons at 18–22px, regular weight, filled for the active nav or tab item.",
      "**Do** give every surface a 1px hairline and, at most, the Rest shadow; reserve Overlay for dialogs and the login card.",
      "**Do** turn tables into stacked cards and dialogs into bottom sheets at 720px and below; keep every task operable by touch.",
      "**Do** keep tap targets at 40px or more and inputs at 16px on phones."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use emoji anywhere in the panel; icons are Phosphor.",
      "**Don't** fill buttons or links with corinto; it is the brand seal and selection marker only.",
      "**Don't** color \"no asistirá\" red; declining is Stone, red is for destructive actions and errors.",
      "**Don't** set controls, numbers or labels in Cormorant Garamond, or use the Display size anywhere but the Respuestas count.",
      "**Don't** return to a dark navy slab background; the panel is light paper.",
      "**Don't** restyle the public invitation from this file; it follows its own Tailwind world."
    ]
  }
}
